# output
# outputs/* (not a bare "outputs/") so the negation below can actually
# re-include one file — git cannot un-ignore a path whose PARENT DIRECTORY
# is itself excluded, only a path excluded by a wildcard on its contents.
outputs/*
# Exception: topic_labels.json is the curated "single source of truth" for
# BERTopic topic labels + parent-theme grouping (docs/TOPIC_WORK_FORWARD_PLAN.md
# M3 calls it "committed" — the blanket outputs/ rule above silently
# prevented that). See docs/TOPIC_MODEL_REFIT_CHECKLIST.md.
!outputs/topic_labels.json

# Exception: the keyword-mediated topic redesign's Phase 4a curation trail
# (the topic-model-redo plan; see CLAUDE.md's "Topic modeling — state of
# play"). topic_keywords.json is the curated single source of truth for the
# Plan B keyword classifier, same treatment as topic_labels.json above.
# keyword_topics.draft.json (the pre-curation editing surface) and
# KEYWORD_REVIEW.md (the human-readable review sheet, src/kw_review_sheet.py)
# are kept alongside it as the human-facing curation record.
# keyword_topics.suggested.json (src/kw_suggest_curation.py) is an assistant
# first-pass review — proposed labels + accept/reject/review calls per
# parent/leaf — kept separate from topic_keywords.json so it's clear which
# file is the human-authored final curation vs. a suggestion to review. The
# larger upstream discovery/comparison artifacts (kw_candidates.json,
# kw_vocab_candidates.json, kw_term_groups_planA.json, kw_term_groups_planB.json,
# kw_stability_planA.json, kw_leaf_assignments_planA.csv) are deliberately
# NOT included here — regenerable via src/kw_discover.py, src/kw_vocab_discover.py,
# src/kw_term_groups.py, src/kw_term_cluster.py, src/kw_stability.py, and not
# worth the repo weight (this project has previously had one large committed
# file account for 25% of .git's pack size — see CLAUDE.md's structure-refactor
# note on docs/TopicVizPrototypes/what_we_can_see.html).
!outputs/topic_keywords.json
!outputs/keyword_topics.draft.json
!outputs/keyword_topics.suggested.json
!outputs/KEYWORD_REVIEW.md

# CI-only publish copies of docs/TopicVizPrototypes/ siblings, created by
# .github/workflows/deploy-notebooks.yml so the prototype pages can fetch()
# their data on GitHub Pages. The real sources are tracked under
# docs/TopicVizPrototypes/{shared,data,what_we_can_see,topic_flow,about}/ —
# committing a second copy here would restore exactly the problem the
# fetch() refactor removed (data/facets.json duplicated and churning on
# every refresh; see docs/TOPIC_MODEL_REFIT_CHECKLIST.md).
docs/onlineoutput/shared/
docs/onlineoutput/data/
docs/onlineoutput/what_we_can_see/
docs/onlineoutput/topic_flow/
docs/onlineoutput/about/

# Processed data artifacts (parquet, pickled frames, etc.) — never commit
data/processed/
*.parquet
*.feather
*.pkl

# Exception: data/nih_nsf_backfill/ pools the NIH RePORTER + NSF Award
# Search backfill outputs (src/backfill_nih_reporter.py,
# src/backfill_nsf_awards.py) — TRACKED deliberately, unlike every other
# *.parquet in the repo. These come from rate-limited external APIs (NIH:
# <=1 req/s; NSF: sequential per-award lookups) and take real wall-clock
# time to regenerate; the raw *_raw.parquet caches in particular are what
# let a parsing bug (e.g. the coPDPI format fix) be reprocessed for free via
# `--offline` instead of re-fetching. Per the *.parquet rule above, a bare
# directory ignore can't be re-included — hence the *.parquet-scoped
# negation, matching the outputs/topic_labels.json exception's pattern.
!data/nih_nsf_backfill/
!data/nih_nsf_backfill/*.parquet

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.vscode/

# Claude Code session logs (local-only)
.claude/sessions/
